    "observed_behavior": "Cashier editor rejects negative profile values for the listed wage fields. The request DTOs carry signed long/nullable-long values. Server create/update handlers validate identity fields, compensation enum and employees_manage permission, then assign compensation values without a server-side nonnegative assertion. Daily wage/overtime/extra-shift paths pass signed values to ledger credits; biometric daily compensation directly posts stored wage; payroll sums credit fields and clamps only final net payable to zero.",
    "classification": "Source-confirmed client/server validation divergence. Negative ledger-credit mechanism source-supported, but business-policy violation and realized payout/loss are not established. Not an authorization bypass.",
    "counterevidence": [
      "Normal cashier form blocks negative values.",
      "Server writes are employees_manage protected.",
      "Zero and null may be legitimate; owner policy is unspecified.",
      "No runtime request, database persistence or payroll settlement was tested."
    ],
